# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

The LKS cluster resource allows you to create and manage LKS (Latitude Kubernetes Service) clusters within your [Latitude.sh](https://latitude.sh/) account. A cluster is the managed control plane; its workers are [`latitudesh_lks_node_pool`](lks_node_pool.md) resources, and a cluster needs at least one node pool to become ready, so create both together, as the example does. See [Clusters](https://www.latitude.sh/docs/lks/clusters) for how clusters work.

`project`, `site` and `network` force a new resource. `name`, `description` and `kubernetes_version` update in place; upgrades are one-way, and the apply waits until the new version is live. Node pools upgrade separately — see [`latitudesh_lks_node_pool`](lks_node_pool.md).

